sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant HS as InactiveAccountCleanupService
    participant US as SqlUserAccountStore
    participant DB as MarsvinDb
    participant ES as IEmailSender
    actor K as Kunde

    Note over HS: BackgroundService started by the host.<br/>Runs once at startup, then every 24 hours.<br/>Implements the storage-limitation rule documented on /Privatliv.

    loop every 24 hours
        HS->>US: DeleteInactiveCustomers(now - 2 years)
        US->>DB: Customer accounts with LastActiveAt before the cutoff
        loop each account
            US->>DB: DeleteUser in one transaction:<br/>PendingLogins, CartItems, Shifts and TimeOffRequests deleted,<br/>Orders.UserId set to NULL, Users row deleted
        end
        Note over HS,DB: Orders survive - UserId is nullable,<br/>so the sales history is kept without a person attached.<br/>Delete runs first, so nobody gets a warning<br/>on the same pass that removes them.

        HS->>US: GetCustomersNeedingInactivityWarning(stage 2: 1 month left)
        loop each account
            HS->>ES: "Din konto slettes om ca. en maaned"<br/>or "...will be deleted in about one month"
            alt mail sent
                HS->>US: SetInactivityWarningStage(userId, 2)
            else sending failed
                Note over HS: Stage left unchanged, so it is retried<br/>on the next run and a warning that never<br/>arrived is not recorded as sent.
            end
        end

        HS->>US: GetCustomersNeedingInactivityWarning(stage 1: 2 months left)
        loop each account
            HS->>ES: "Din konto slettes om ca. to maaneder"<br/>or "...will be deleted in about two months"
            HS->>US: SetInactivityWarningStage(userId, 1)
        end
    end

    K->>US: any successful login (ConfirmLogin or VerifyTotp)
    US->>DB: RecordActivity: LastActiveAt = now, InactivityWarningStage = 0
    Note over K,DB: Logging in once is all it takes to keep the account.

    Note over HS,ES: No browser is involved, so each warning is written in<br/>Users.PrefersEnglish - the language the account last used.<br/>Only Customer accounts are in scope.<br/>Employee and Admin accounts are never auto-deleted.<br/>An exception in one run is logged, and the next run tries again.
